    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0303" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/7–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Livengood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d214-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-26T16:00:00+08:00">July 26, 1948—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>653. Abbey saw Hatta evening July 25 and communicated gist of Department’s
                        telegram,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d214-f2"/> except last paragraph. Hatta
                    confirmed suspension political negotiations only to last until Dutch Cabinet
                    resumed. He fears that it may be some time before Dutch Cabinet can be formed.
                    He appeared to understand Department’s position fully. With regard to Tuesday’s
                    meeting SC, Hatta said Palar already fully informed and instructed. He
                    reiterated this when queried again later <pb facs="0304" n="290" xml:id="pg290"
                    /> in conversation, the indication being Palar will not submit any untoward
                    statement in the premise.</p>
                <p>Hatta expressed concern for immediate signing of agreements, appeared more
                    affable and expansive than usual.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livengood</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
